# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

## Summary
Successfully configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation.

## What Was Implemented

### 1. Analytics Integration
- Added the `<Analytics />` component from `@vercel/analytics/next` to the root layout
- Integrated according to the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide for Next.js App Router

### 2. Files Modified
- **src/app/layout.jsx**
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag (after GoogleAnalytics)

### 3. Package Information
- The `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) was already installed in package.json
- No additional package installation was required
- Dependencies were verified and the project was successfully built

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Approach
- Identified this as a Next.js App Router project
- Followed the App Router integration pattern (adding to root layout)
- Placed the Analytics component at the end of the body element, following best practices

### Code Placement
The Analytics component was added after the existing GoogleAnalytics component to maintain consistency with the project's analytics setup structure.

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ Fetched latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
✅ Installed dependencies (npm install)
✅ Ran linter (eslint) - No errors
✅ Built the project successfully (npm run build)
✅ Verified 166 static pages generated without errors
✅ Staged only the necessary source code changes

## Next Steps for Deployment

To activate Vercel Web Analytics:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
2. Deploy this change to production using `vercel deploy` or through Git integration
3. Verify the integration by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

## Notes
- The Analytics component is lightweight and will only send data when deployed on Vercel
- In local development, the component renders but does not track events
- No additional configuration or environment variables are needed
- The package was already present, so no lock file updates were required
